%% Product requests and delivery-personnel operational flow
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Customer
    participant Web as Customer Web/BFF
    participant RequestAPI as Product request API
    participant DB as Tenant PostgreSQL
    participant Admin as Tenant admin
    participant RiderWeb as Rider portal/BFF
    participant RiderAPI as Delivery personnel API
    participant Courier as Order/assignment service

    Customer->>Web: Submit product request
    Web->>RequestAPI: Public request with validated bounded fields
    RequestAPI->>DB: Create tenant-local product request
    DB-->>Web: Accepted request reference

    Admin->>RequestAPI: List/filter product requests
    RequestAPI->>DB: Apply status/page bounds
    DB-->>Admin: Count-plus-page envelope
    Admin->>RequestAPI: Update status or delete request
    RequestAPI->>DB: Apply admin role/permission/membership checks
    DB-->>Admin: Audited request transition

    RiderWeb->>RiderAPI: Submit rider credentials through login BFF
    RiderAPI->>Courier: Validate rider identity and tenant assignment
    Courier-->>RiderWeb: HTTP-only rider session cookie
    RiderWeb->>RiderAPI: Read assigned orders or online status
    RiderAPI->>Courier: Verify rider token and assignment ownership
    Courier->>DB: Read/update tenant delivery state
    DB-->>RiderWeb: Allowed rider projection

    RiderWeb->>RiderAPI: Update assigned order status/location
    RiderAPI->>Courier: Validate status transition and assigned rider
    Courier->>DB: Persist delivery evidence and order history
    Courier-->>RiderWeb: Stable update result

    Note over RequestAPI,DB: Public callers cannot list, mutate, or enumerate admin requests.
    Note over RiderWeb,RiderAPI: Raw rider JWT stays in an HTTP-only cookie and is not exposed to client JavaScript.
    Note over Courier,DB: Rider identity and order assignment are checked server-side, not trusted from the browser.
